<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="SelectVerdict's privacy policy and current approach to data collection."><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} /><PageIntro eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy" description="A plain-language account of the information this website currently handles." /><article class="section narrow prose"><p class="meta"><strong>Effective:</strong> August 31, 2026</p><h2>Information we collect</h2><p>SelectVerdict does not currently provide accounts, forms, comments, or on-site purchases, and we do not intentionally collect personal information through those features. Our hosting provider may process basic request data such as IP address, browser information, requested pages, and timestamps to deliver and secure the website.</p><h2>Cookies and analytics</h2><p>We do not currently include advertising pixels or third-party analytics scripts. If that changes, this policy will be updated and any consent mechanism required by applicable law will be provided.</p><h2>External and affiliate links</h2><p>Links may take you to third-party websites with their own privacy practices. Some may be affiliate links, as explained in our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p><h2>Data sharing and retention</h2><p>We do not sell personal information. Infrastructure providers may process limited technical data on our behalf and retain it according to their operational and security policies.</p><h2>Your rights and contact</h2><p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights concerning personal information. Contact details for privacy requests will be added before any feature that intentionally collects such information launches.</p><h2>Changes</h2><p>We may revise this policy as the site changes. The effective date above identifies the current version.</p></article></BaseLayout>
